{
  "title": "Dua when you see a Diseased or Defected Person",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "Twenty-third: Imam Muhammad al-Baqir (a) is reported to have said: whenever you see a diseased or defected person, repeat this saying three times inaudibly, without letting him hear you. If you do so, you will not be affected by that disease or defect:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ عَافَانِىْ مِمَّا ابْتَلَاكَ بِهٖ وَ لَوْ شَاۤءَ فَعَلَ\nALHAMDULILLAAHIL LAZEE A'AFAANEE MIMMAB TALAAKA BIHI WA LAW SHAAA-A FA-A'L\nPraise be to Allah, Who has kept me well from what He has afflicted you with — and had He willed, He would have done so [to me too].\nAccording to another tradition, the following statement should be said in such situations:\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ عَافَانِىْ مِمَّا ابْتَلَاكَ بِهٖ وَ فَضَّلَنِىْ عَلَيْكَ وَ عَلٰى كَثِيْرٍ مِمَّنْ خَلَقَ\nALHAMDULILLAAHIL LAZEE A'AFAANEE MIMMAB TALAAKA BIHI WA FADDALANEE A'LAYKA WA A'LAA KASEERIM MIMMAN KHALAQ\nPraise be to Allah, Who has kept me well from what He has afflicted you with, and has favored me above you and above many of those whom He has created.\nIt is also required to say this statement as inaudibly as possible, so that the defected person does not hear you."
}
